NV_PK(39,{"opened in 2011 and designed by the japanese architect norihiko dan two curving concrete wings frame the lake like a picture it is free with clean restrooms":"","the 4 kilometer stretch from shuishe to xiangshan floats on a boardwalk just above the water in 2012 cnngo listed the lake's bikeway among the ten most beautiful in the world":"","it worships civil and martial gods under one roof it was rebuilt in 1969 after the rising water covered two older temples in a northern palace style with red columns and yellow tiles":"","two stone lions at the entrance about 8 meters tall donated in 1981 they are a good photo instead of the god statues":"","the sacred center of the thao and home of their highest ancestral spirit the 1999 earthquake made it much smaller no one may land there":"","work began in 1919 under japanese rule it raised the water about 18 meters and joined two smaller lakes into one the lake is a working reservoir":"","every september since 1983 more than 20 000 swimmers cross about 3 3 kilometers of the lake it is taiwan's largest open water event":"","a local woman has sold eggs simmered in shiitake and tea here since the 1980s describe the smell not just the price":"","it keeps a relic of xuanzang the tang dynasty monk who brought buddhist scriptures back from india the relic came to taiwan in 1965":"","finished in 1971 chiang kai shek built it in memory of his mother it is 46 meters high and its tip is exactly 1 000 meters above sea level":"","brought from india to yuchi in 1925 under japanese rule the altitude the mist and the acidic soil here are like northeast india":"","taiwan tea no 18 released in 1999 it is a cross of burmese large leaf tea and taiwanese wild tea with an aroma of cinnamon and mint":"","assam tea was brought from india in 1925":"","the swimming carnival has been held since 1983":"","norihiko dan's visitor center of 2011 with a sky deck 30 meters over the water the best rainy day stop":"","yuchi township assam tea since 1925 ruby black tea and the tea research station":"","the 1980s":"","sun moon lake is natural in origin but engineered in its present form from 1919 to 1934 a hydroelectric scheme raised the water about 18 meters and joined two smaller lakes into one in 1925 assam tea seeds from india were planted around yuchi":"","after the war temples and monuments rose around the lake wenwu temple was rebuilt in 1969 ci'en pagoda was finished in 1971 and the first swimming carnival crossed the lake in 1983":"","in 1999 the 921 earthquake made lalu island much smaller in 2000 the national scenic area was set up and dehuashe became ita thao in 2001 the thao were recognized as taiwan's 11th indigenous nation":"","new attractions came quickly the year steps in 2003 the ropeway in 2009 and the xiangshan visitor center in 2011 in 2012 cnngo praised the bikeway and that changed the local economy":"","be honest about what is ancient and what is recent the year steps are from 2003 the ropeway from 2009 and the lake's present shape from the 1930s guests trust a guide who separates the two":"","xiangshan visitor center opened in 2011":"","wenwu temple was rebuilt in 1969":"","assam tea came to yuchi in 1925":""});